From 88dabc8f501155d4193e06c33e2d6b8669daf010 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 07:10:38 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 22/48] v4.7-gpu: convert Infinity stat counters to per-CPU
 atomics

The global atomic stat counters are incremented from every CPU (the
EMA climb counter on every tick).  On multi-node machines this bounces
a single cache line across sockets at tick rate, adding measurable
cross-socket coherence traffic on large systems.

Convert all 13 counters to per-CPU atomics: hot increments stay local
to the running CPU, and the stats handler sums all CPUs via a helper.
The unsigned-int cast in the helper preserves the 32-bit wrap semantics
of atomic_read(), and the 64-bit sum keeps the displayed totals exact
for far longer than a single 32-bit counter on 24/7 systems.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
---
